al therapy in HIV-infected patients: the Swiss HIV Cohort Study.</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>392</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16540942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000552-Carrieri1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carrieri</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Leport</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Protopopescu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cassuto</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouvet</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Factors associated with nonadherence to highly active antiretroviral therapy: a 5-year follow-up analysis with correction for the bias induced by missing data in the treatment maintenance phase.</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>485</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16652057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000552-Bartlett1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bartlett</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Addressing the challenges of adherence.</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr</source><volume>29</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S2</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11832696</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000552-Murri1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murri</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ammassari</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Trotta</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>De</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><s